@startuml
!include ../common/style.puml

title HANBAY HOTEL - Concurrent Booking Prevention

autonumber

actor "Guest A" as GuestA
actor "Guest B" as GuestB
boundary "Booking API A" as APIA
boundary "Booking API B" as APIB
control "Booking Service A" as ServiceA
control "Booking Service B" as ServiceB
database "Room Type Repository" as RoomTypeRepo
database "Booking Repository" as BookingRepo
database "PostgreSQL" as DB

par Guest A creates booking
    GuestA -> APIA: POST /bookings
    APIA -> ServiceA: createBooking()
and Guest B creates booking
    GuestB -> APIB: POST /bookings
    APIB -> ServiceB: createBooking()
end

ServiceA -> RoomTypeRepo: findByIdForUpdate(roomTypeId)
RoomTypeRepo -> DB: SELECT room_type FOR UPDATE
DB --> RoomTypeRepo: Lock acquired by transaction A
RoomTypeRepo --> ServiceA: Locked room type

ServiceB -> RoomTypeRepo: findByIdForUpdate(roomTypeId)
RoomTypeRepo -> DB: SELECT room_type FOR UPDATE

note right of DB
Transaction B waits until
transaction A releases the lock.
end note

ServiceA -> BookingRepo: countOverlappingBookings()
BookingRepo -> DB: Count active overlapping bookings
DB --> BookingRepo: 0 occupied
BookingRepo --> ServiceA: 1 room available

ServiceA -> BookingRepo: Save PENDING booking A
BookingRepo -> DB: INSERT booking A
DB --> BookingRepo: Success
ServiceA -> DB: COMMIT and release lock
ServiceA --> APIA: Booking created
APIA --> GuestA: 201 Created

DB --> RoomTypeRepo: Transaction B acquires lock
RoomTypeRepo --> ServiceB: Locked room type

ServiceB -> BookingRepo: countOverlappingBookings()
BookingRepo -> DB: Count active overlapping bookings
DB --> BookingRepo: 1 occupied
BookingRepo --> ServiceB: 0 rooms available

ServiceB -> ServiceB: Roll back transaction
ServiceB --> APIB: BOOKING_001
APIB --> GuestB: 409 Conflict

note over ServiceA, DB
The availability re-check must happen after acquiring
the lock and inside the booking transaction.
end note

@enduml
